Q: Unable to generate audio element on an HTML page using JavaScript A: <p>I fixed the issue by changing [&quot;audioClip&quot;, new Audio(&quot;audiofiles/hawaiian0.mp3&quot;)] to [&quot;audioClip&quot;, &quot;audiofiles/hawaiian0.mp3&quot;]</p>
<p>The final JavaScript code is as follows:</p>
<pre><code>const hawaiian = new Map([
    [&quot;langName&quot;, &quot;Hawaiian&quot;],
    [&quot;audioClip&quot;, &quot;audiofiles/hawaiian0.mp3&quot;],
    [&quot;langFamily&quot;, &quot;Austronesian&quot;],
    [&quot;infoBlurb&quot;, &quot;Hawaiian is a polynesian language spoken in Hawaii&quot;]
]);

function playButtonClicked(){
    const audioPlayer = document.createElement('audio');
    audioPlayer.controls=true;
    audioPlayer.src=hawaiian.get('audioClip');
    audioPlayer.type=&quot;audio/mpeg&quot;;
    document.getElementById(&quot;audioPlayerID&quot;).appendChild(audioPlayer);
}

document.querySelector(&quot;#playButton&quot;).onclick = playButtonClicked;
</code></pre>

Q: &#39;data:image/jpg;base64&#39; and jQuery image preview in Internet Explorer A: <p>I already have a problem like this. The main reason for this incompatibility is the <code>runat="server"</code> attribute in the image tag and maybe in the anchor tag. Try this, maybe your problem will be solved:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;
    $(function () {
        $('#gallery a').lightBox({ fixedNavigation: true });
    });
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;div id="mainDiv" runat="server"&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>And in <a href="http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/code-behind" rel="nofollow">code behind</a>:</p>

<pre><code>...
string innerHtml = "&lt;div id='gallery'&gt;&lt;a id='aPhoto'&gt;&lt;img alt='photo' id='imgPhoto' /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;";
mainDiv.innerHtml = innerHtml;
...
</code></pre>
